I am at the citizens' registration office today.
It is early on Tuesday morning.
I have an appointment for my registration here.
Many people are already here.
I sit and wait.
I have a waiting number.
My number is eighty-nine.
A screen on the wall shows the numbers.
I look at the screen.
It shows the number eighty-two.
I calculate briefly in my head.
Seven people are still ahead of me.
I have all the documents in my backpack.
I need the passport for the registration.
I look at the screen again.
It now shows the number eighty-three.
So only six people are still waiting ahead of me.
I still have enough time before work.
Soon it is my turn.
